Cell["\<\
When the building blocks are simple but the routine is hairy, this interface \
can read more concise than explicit procedural code.\
\>", "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"750b1aa6-39a6-f84f-92e2-390fa828e503"],

Cell["\<\
Does it feel intuitive or idiomatic? Is the programming interface awkward?\
\>", "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"c4a31e00-b550-ef45-b4ed-c48771d3e0c5"],

Cell["\<\
The project is still in extremely early stage, and I\[CloseCurlyQuote]m \
struggling to get the interface consistent and the documentation synced.\
\[LineSeparator]I think it won\[CloseCurlyQuote]t take long to run into rough \
edges when trying it out, but I will keep trying to improve it!\
\>", "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"d230f274-f8e2-c44d-b409-1b74d416fb7d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Motivation", "Section",
ExpressionUUID->"32fae459-fede-934e-90d4-ca299517bbb9"],

Cell["\<\
A lot of image processing and machine learning techniques rely on structured \
manipulations of multi-dimensional arrays, or loosely, tensors. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4a92b59a-5dd0-0142-9269-7dccdd2805f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Being a list-native language, Wolfram Language has a ",
 ButtonBox["plethora",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:guide/HandlingArraysOfData"],
 " of convenient and performant primitives to handle multi-dimensional \
arrays;\[LineSeparator]and, even better, these built-in functions almost \
always work smoothly with any representation of arrays,\[LineSeparator]no \
matter if they are ",
 ButtonBox["nested-lists",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:tutorial/ManipulatingLists#15721"],
 " with all M-expression flexibility, ",
 ButtonBox["symbolic tensors",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:guide/SymbolicTensors"],
 ", declarative and efficient ",
 ButtonBox["sparse arrays",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:https://guide/SparseArrays"],
 ", or ",
 ButtonBox["packed",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/compiledtype/PackedArray"],
 " ",
 ButtonBox["objects",
  BaseStyle->"Link",
  ButtonData->"paclet:ref/NumericArray"],
 " that have native speed."
}], "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"6054ed84-20b4-a245-95fc-28b9badb8cc4"],

Cell["\<\
With batching, striding, resampling and so on, array data can often contain \
dimensions that are mapped over rather than operated upon, and these can \
often need joining, splitting or recombining on the fly; even when the \
individual operations are simple, the imperative flow of code can often grow \
hard to reason about, requiring verbose variable names, comments, and \
exterior documentation.\
\>", "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"2edf3562-6533-7c4d-81d9-93b17164c943"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Einstein notation", "Subsection",
ExpressionUUID->"6e0e2970-2c6b-0b44-84d4-0d4d3e54a922"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For linear algebraic operations, the ",
 ButtonBox["Einstein summation",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Einstein_notation"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Einstein_notation"],
 " convention is a great convenience; mathematicians and physicians enjoy it \
so much that they extended it into ",
 ButtonBox["Ricci calculus",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ricci_calculus"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ricci_calculus"],
 " and ",
 ButtonBox["abstract index notation",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_index_notation"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_index_notation"],
 ". Programmers tapped into it as well:"
}], "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"cfffc6d3-6b6d-b245-8b66-98412b0fb6bc"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"a", "=", 
   RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", "6", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"b", "=", 
   RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", "12", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"4", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"b", ".", "a"}], ")"}], "\[Transpose]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"60f3b4ce-2fd9-5143-82a7-b92cef545b6c"],

