examples"],
 ";"
}], "Item",
ExpressionUUID->"f1c6220d-8700-cf45-9142-d1d0578bd9ba"],

Cell["\<\
Within-tensor contraction (generalized traces) and diagonal extraction\
\>", "Item",
ExpressionUUID->"d479f94c-5a1b-364f-80a6-45958a47bf69"],

Cell["\<\
and many stuff that are more obvious but still not yet implemented.\
\>", "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"0ef9c1c1-e7bc-9447-903c-fd9ef6280cb5"],

Cell["\<\
Though, the goal is not to clone einops or einx feature-for-feature either; \
\[LineSeparator]I am more interested in whether tensor-axis notation can be \
made to feel idiomatic in Wolfram Language: \[LineSeparator]using pattern \
bindings for inferred dimensions, symbolic expressions as an AST, and the \
existing array primitives as the lowering targets.
I hope this makes more able people find this interesting or worth looking \
into.\
\>", "Text",
ExpressionUUID->"7d044b58-a98d-f743-8217-adbbfc7fb829"],

